    <bpmn:process id="W_W1218" name="W1218. Intercompany Service Agreement Annual Review, Rate Adjustment &amp; Renewal" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual review date (Q4 each year); or triggered by material cost change in intercompany service delivery; or triggered by BIR transfer pricing documentation requirement
Frequency: Annual comprehensive review; quarterly rate monitoring
Volume: ~8–12 intercompany service agreements across 5 legal entities
Owner: Controller
Participants: Controller, CFO, Legal Counsel, COO, DC Manager (BuildRight Logistics), GM, Digital Commerce Inc. (BuildRight Digital Commerce), Property Manager (BuildRight Property Management)
Source: workflow W1218 — Intercompany Service Agreement Annual Review, Rate Adjustment &amp; Renewal</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1218_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1218_Lane1" name="Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1218_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1218_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1218_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1218_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1218_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1218_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1218_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1218_Lane2" name="Legal Counsel">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1218_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1218_Lane3" name="Finance Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1218_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1218_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1218_Start5" name="Annual review date (Q4 each year); or triggered by material cost change in intercompany…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1218_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1218_Task6" name="Annual review initiation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Annual review initiation (October): Controller sends review notice to all intercompany service providers and recipients: (a) list of all active IC service agreements with current terms and rates, (b) request cost data from service providers: actual cost of service delivery for trailing 12 months (labor, overhead, allocated costs), (c) request volume data from service recipients: actual volumes consumed vs. contracted volumes
Responsible (R): Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1218_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1218_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1218_Task7" name="Cost analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Cost analysis: Controller analyzes each IC service: (a) Warehousing/distribution fees (Logistics → Depot): actual DC operating cost per sqm and per pallet vs. current rate; compare to third-party warehousing market rates (arm&#x27;s-length benchmark); (b) Ecommerce fulfillment fees (Digital Commerce → Depot): actual platform operating cost per order vs. current per-order fee; compare to third-party fulfillment center rates; (c) Property lease rates (Property Management → Depot): actual property cost (depreciation, property tax, maintenance) vs. current lease rate; compare to commercial lease rates in each location; (d) Shared services allocation (Holdings → all entities): actual HQ department costs allocated per agreed methodology (headcount-based, revenue-based, or usage-based)
Responsible (R): Controller / Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1218_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1218_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1218_Task8" name="Arm&#x27;s-length benchmarking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Arm&#x27;s-length benchmarking: Controller engages external transfer pricing advisor (or uses internal benchmarking database) to: (a) identify comparable third-party transactions or service providers in the Philippine market, (b) apply acceptable TP methods: CUP (Comparable Uncontrolled Price) for lease rates, Cost Plus for service fees, TNMM (Transactional Net Margin Method) for complex arrangements, (c) document benchmarking analysis per BIR RR 02-2013 requirements
Responsible (R): Controller / TP Advisor
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1218_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1218_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1218_Task9" name="Rate adjustment proposal">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Rate adjustment proposal: Controller proposes rate adjustments: (a) where actual costs deviate &gt; 10% from current rates: propose adjustment (increase or decrease), (b) where benchmarking shows current rates outside arm&#x27;s-length range: propose adjustment to bring within range, (c) where volumes changed significantly: propose volume-based rate tier adjustments, (d) document proposed rates with supporting analysis
Responsible (R): Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1218_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1218_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1218_Task10" name="Stakeholder review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Stakeholder review: Controller presents proposed rates to service provider and recipient entity heads: (a) DC Manager (Logistics) reviews warehousing rate, (b) GM, Digital Commerce Inc. (Digital Commerce) reviews fulfillment fee, (c) Property Manager reviews lease rates, (d) COO reviews impact on Depot, Inc. operating costs; negotiate and agree on rates
Responsible (R): Controller / Entity Heads
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1218_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1218_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1218_Task11" name="Legal documentation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Legal documentation: Legal Counsel drafts updated service agreements: (a) updated rates and effective dates, (b) volume commitments and minimums, (c) SLA terms, (d) termination clauses, (e) BIR compliance provisions (TP documentation reference); both entity signatories execute agreements
Responsible (R): Legal Counsel
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1218_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1218_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1218_Task12" name="System update">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: System update: Finance Analyst updates ERP intercompany pricing: (a) new service rates effective January 1, (b) updated allocation methodologies in cost allocation module, (c) updated IC revenue/expense accounts per entity, (d) updated transfer pricing documentation file per W235
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst / System
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1218_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1218_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1218_Task13" name="BIR transfer pricing documentation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: BIR transfer pricing documentation: Controller files BIR Form 1709 (Transfer Pricing Documentation) with Annual Income Tax Return per W235; includes: (a) organizational structure, (b) description of IC transactions, (c) TP method applied and benchmarking analysis, (d) financial results of IC transactions, (e) updated service agreements as supporting documents
Responsible (R): Controller / Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Annual filing per W235</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1218_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1218_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1218_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1218_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1218_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-290 (ensure controlled execution — Consolidation &amp; Intercompany (PA-17.2).) | - operational: Controller review and approval gate
Owner: Controller</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1218_Assoc16" sourceRef="W1218_Annotation15" targetRef="W1218_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1218_Flow17" sourceRef="W1218_Start5" targetRef="W1218_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1218_Flow18" sourceRef="W1218_Task6" targetRef="W1218_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1218_Flow19" sourceRef="W1218_Task7" targetRef="W1218_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1218_Flow20" sourceRef="W1218_Task8" targetRef="W1218_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1218_Flow21" sourceRef="W1218_Task9" targetRef="W1218_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1218_Flow22" sourceRef="W1218_Task10" targetRef="W1218_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1218_Flow23" sourceRef="W1218_Task11" targetRef="W1218_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1218_Flow24" sourceRef="W1218_Task12" targetRef="W1218_Task13" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1218_Flow25" sourceRef="W1218_Task13" targetRef="W1218_End14" />
    </bpmn:process>
