    <bpmn:process id="W_W1277" name="W1277. Intercompany Warehouse Service Fee Monthly Calculation, Billing &amp; Reconciliation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly close cycle; BuildRight Logistics, Inc. DC operations data available (T+3)
Frequency: Monthly
Volume: 4 DCs operated by BuildRight Logistics, Inc. providing warehousing and distribution services to BuildRight Depot, Inc.; ~50,000 replenishment orders/month (production-calibrated per data-volumes §1.1); ~6,000 goods receipts/month
Owner: Logistics Finance Analyst
Participants: Logistics Finance Analyst, Controller (BuildRight Logistics), AP Manager (BuildRight Depot), DC Managers (4)
Source: workflow W1277 — Intercompany Warehouse Service Fee Monthly Calculation, Billing &amp; Reconciliation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1277_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1277_Lane1" name="DC Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1277_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1277_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1277_Lane2" name="Logistics Finance Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1277_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1277_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1277_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1277_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1277_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1277_Lane4" name="AP Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1277_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1277_Lane5" name="Treasury Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1277_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1277_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1277_Start7" name="Monthly close cycle; BuildRight Logistics, Inc. DC operations data available (T+3)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1277_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1277_Task8" name="Monthly DC activity data collection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly DC activity data collection: by T+3 after month-end, each DC Manager submits monthly activity report: (a) Inbound volume: number of goods receipts, total pallets received, total units received, number of import containers devanned (W1271), (b) Outbound volume: number of store shipments, total pallets shipped, total units shipped, number of delivery stops, (c) Storage activity: pallet-days of storage (inventory on hand × days in month), peak storage utilization %, (d) Value-added services: number of kits assembled (W46), number of cross-dock operations (W221/W1226), number of special handling requests (hazmat per W1222, temperature-controlled per W1029), (e) Labor hours: total DC labor hours, overtime hours, contract/temp labor hours
Responsible (R): DC Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 2 hours/DC</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1277_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1277_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1277_Task9" name="Service fee calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Service fee calculation: Logistics Finance Analyst calculates monthly IC warehouse service fee per DC using the rate structure agreed in W612: (a) Fixed component (monthly base fee): covers DC rent, depreciation, core staff salaries — fixed per DC per month regardless of volume, (b) Variable — Receiving fee: per-pallet or per-unit rate × actual inbound volume, (c) Variable — Storage fee: per-pallet-day rate × actual pallet-days of storage, (d) Variable — Shipping fee: per-shipment rate × actual outbound shipments + per-stop rate × actual delivery stops, (e) Variable — Value-added fee: per-activity rate × actual VA activities performed, (f) Variable — Special handling surcharge: premium rate for hazmat, temperature-controlled, and oversized items, (g) Total monthly service fee per DC = (a) + (b) + (c) + (d) + (e) + (f); calculated for each of 4 DCs
Responsible (R): Logistics Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): Controller (Logistics)
Duration: 3–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1277_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1277_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1277_Task10" name="Service fee invoice generation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Service fee invoice generation: system generates IC service invoice per DC: (a) invoice from BuildRight Logistics, Inc. (service provider) to BuildRight Depot, Inc. (service recipient), (b) line items matching fee components from step 2, (c) VAT (12%) added per Philippine tax law — IC services are subject to VAT, (d) supporting detail: DC activity report (step 1), rate table per W612, calculation worksheet, (e) BIR-compliant invoice format with sequential invoice number per entity&#x27;s registered CAS (W1181)
Responsible (R): System / Logistics Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): Controller (Logistics)
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1277_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1277_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1277_Task11" name="Depot Inc. validation and approval">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Depot Inc. validation and approval: AP Manager (BuildRight Depot, Inc.) receives IC service invoices for all 4 DCs; validates: (a) total fee is within ±10% of budgeted amount per W26 — if &gt; 10% variance, Logistics Finance Analyst provides explanation (volume surge, seasonal peak, special projects), (b) activity data is consistent with Depot&#x27;s own transaction data: number of store replenishment orders (W4), goods receipts at stores, intercompany transfers, (c) rates match current IC agreement per W612, (d) VAT calculation verified; AP Manager approves for payment or returns with queries
Responsible (R): AP Manager
Accountable (A): CFO (Depot)
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1277_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1277_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1277_Task12" name="IC journal entry posting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: IC journal entry posting: once approved, system posts IC entries: (a) BuildRight Depot, Inc.: debit — warehousing/distribution expense (COGS component), debit — input VAT (12%), credit — IC payable to BuildRight Logistics, Inc., (b) BuildRight Logistics, Inc.: debit — IC receivable from BuildRight Depot, Inc., credit — IC warehousing service revenue, credit — output VAT (12%), (c) entries posted to respective entity GLs with IC flag for consolidation elimination per W234
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1277_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1277_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1277_Task13" name="Monthly reconciliation and variance analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Monthly reconciliation and variance analysis: Logistics Finance Analyst prepares monthly IC warehouse fee reconciliation: (a) actual fees vs. budget (W26) with variance explanation, (b) cost per unit handled (total fee ÷ total units processed) — tracked for productivity monitoring, (c) cost per store delivery (shipping component ÷ number of deliveries), (d) storage utilization vs. capacity — underutilized DCs flagged for review, (e) comparison across 4 DCs — identify outliers (DC with significantly higher cost per unit may have efficiency issues), (f) reconciliation report shared with VP Supply Chain and CFO for monthly business review
Responsible (R): Logistics Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain / CFO
Duration: 2–3 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1277_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1277_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1277_Task14" name="Settlement execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Settlement execution: approved IC service fees settled per W1201 monthly IC settlement batch processing — netted against other IC transactions between Depot Inc. and Logistics Inc. (including any Logistics Inc. payments to Depot Inc. for shared services) to determine net IC payable amount; net amount settled via intercompany bank transfer
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: Per W1201</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1277_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1277_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1277_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1277_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1277_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-290 (ensure controlled execution — Consolidation &amp; Intercompany (PA-17.2).) | - operational: Logistics Finance Analyst review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Logistics Finance Analyst</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
