    <bpmn:process id="W_W1293" name="W1293. Multi-Entity Intercompany Service Fee Billing &amp; Settlement" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly intercompany service fee billing cycle; or quarterly settlement reconciliation
Frequency: Monthly billing; monthly settlement netting per W1201/W14
Volume: ~15–20 active IC service fee arrangements across 5 entities; ~60–80 IC invoices per month
Owner: Corporate Controller
Participants: Corporate Controller, Entity Accountants (5 entities), Treasury, AP, AR
Source: workflow W1293 — Multi-Entity Intercompany Service Fee Billing &amp; Settlement</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1293_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1293_Lane1" name="Entity Accountants">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1293_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1293_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1293_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1293_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1293_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1293_Lane3" name="Treasury">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1293_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1293_Lane4" name="Corporate Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1293_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1293_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1293_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1293_Start6" name="Monthly intercompany service fee billing cycle; or quarterly settlement reconciliation">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1293_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1293_Task7" name="Monthly IC fee calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly IC fee calculation: Entity Accountants calculate monthly IC service fees based on contracted terms: (a) Logistics: warehousing fee per pallet position + distribution fee per delivery + handling fee per unit × actual volumes for the month, (b) Digital Commerce: platform fee per ecommerce order + payment processing fee per transaction + fulfillment fee per BOPIS order, (c) Property Management: monthly lease per location per signed lease agreement, (d) Holdings: management fee (percentage of subsidiary revenue per service agreement); system auto-calculates fees from transactional data where possible
Responsible (R): Entity Accountants / System
Accountable (A): Corporate Controller
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1293_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1293_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1293_Task8" name="IC invoice generation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: IC invoice generation: System generates IC invoices: (a) BIR-compliant invoice format with IC indicator, (b) service description, period, quantity, rate, and amount, (c) supporting schedule with calculation detail (e.g., number of deliveries × rate per delivery = total), (d) WHT calculation per BIR requirements (expanded withholding tax on service fees), (e) IC invoice auto-recorded in both issuing entity&#x27;s AR and receiving entity&#x27;s AP
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Corporate Controller
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1293_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1293_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1293_Task9" name="IC invoice approval &amp; posting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: IC invoice approval &amp; posting: Entity Accountants review IC invoices: (a) verify calculation accuracy against contracted rates and actual volumes, (b) verify supporting documentation (delivery reports, order counts, lease agreements), (c) post IC invoice in respective entity books: debit in receiving entity (expense), credit in issuing entity (revenue), (d) system auto-creates IC elimination entries for consolidated reporting per W14
Responsible (R): Entity Accountants
Accountable (A): Corporate Controller
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1293_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1293_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1293_Task10" name="Quarterly IC settlement netting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quarterly IC settlement netting: Treasury performs quarterly IC settlement: (a) system nets all IC payables and receivables across 5 entities, (b) calculates net settlement amount per entity (net payer or net receiver), (c) for net payable entities: schedule bank transfer to net receivable entities, (d) record settlement transactions: debit IC payable / credit bank (payer), debit bank / credit IC receivable (receiver), (e) verify IC balances are fully settled or documented for carry-forward
Responsible (R): Treasury / Corporate Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1293_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1293_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1293_Task11" name="Transfer pricing documentation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Transfer pricing documentation: Corporate Controller maintains transfer pricing documentation: (a) update benchmarking analysis annually per BIR RR 02-2013, as supplemented by RR 19-2020 (TPD/Form 1709), (b) document arm&#x27;s-length basis for each IC fee arrangement (comparable market rates, cost-plus methodology, or transactional net margin method), (c) maintain contemporaneous documentation file for BIR audit readiness per W77, (d) engage external transfer pricing advisor for annual review
Responsible (R): Corporate Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 8 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1293_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1293_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1293_Task12" name="IC reconciliation &amp; audit trail">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: IC reconciliation &amp; audit trail: Monthly, Corporate Controller reconciles IC balances: (a) verify IC receivable in Entity A = IC payable in Entity B for each arrangement, (b) investigate and resolve any mismatches (timing differences, calculation errors, missing invoices), (c) ensure all IC balances are properly eliminated in consolidated trial balance per W14, (d) maintain IC audit trail for external auditors (SGV, Isla Lipana, or equivalent)
Responsible (R): Corporate Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1293_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1293_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1293_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1293_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1293_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-290 (ensure controlled execution — Consolidation &amp; Intercompany (PA-17.2).) | - operational: Corporate Controller review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Corporate Controller</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1293_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1293_Annotation14" targetRef="W1293_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
