    <bpmn:process id="W_W1299" name="W1299. Intercompany Transfer Pricing Review, Adjustment &amp; Arm&#x27;s-Length Compliance Documentation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual transfer pricing review cycle; or regulatory audit notification (BIR); or significant change in intercompany transaction volumes or pricing
Frequency: Annual comprehensive review; quarterly monitoring; ad-hoc for pricing adjustments
Volume: 5 legal entities; IC flows per W612/W1293 (warehousing, ecommerce platform, property leasing, management fees); estimated PHP 2–3B in annual intercompany transactions
Owner: Finance Controller
Participants: Finance Controller, CFO, Tax Accountant, VP Legal &amp; Compliance, External Transfer Pricing Advisor
Source: workflow W1299 — Intercompany Transfer Pricing Review, Adjustment &amp; Arm&#x27;s-Length Compliance Documentation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1299_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1299_Lane1" name="Finance Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1299_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1299_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1299_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1299_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1299_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1299_Lane2" name="External Transfer Pricing Advisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1299_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1299_Lane3" name="VP Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1299_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1299_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1299_Start5" name="Annual transfer pricing review cycle; or regulatory audit notification (BIR); or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1299_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1299_Task6" name="Annual intercompany transaction mapping">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Annual intercompany transaction mapping: Finance Controller compiles comprehensive map of all intercompany transactions: (a) transaction type (service fee, lease, management fee, goods transfer), (b) paying entity and receiving entity, (c) annual transaction volume and value, (d) current pricing methodology (cost-plus, comparable uncontrolled price, transactional net margin method), (e) prior year transfer pricing documentation and benchmarking study results
Responsible (R): Finance Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1–2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1299_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1299_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1299_Task7" name="Benchmarking study update">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Benchmarking study update: External Transfer Pricing Advisor updates benchmarking analysis: (a) identify comparable independent transactions in Philippine market (e.g., third-party warehouse rental rates, third-party ecommerce platform fees, third-party logistics rates), (b) apply transfer pricing methods per BIR guidelines: (i) Cost-Plus Method: intercompany fee = cost × (1 + arm&#x27;s-length markup %) — used for warehousing and logistics services, (ii) Comparable Uncontrolled Price Method: compare to market rates — used for property leases, (iii) Transactional Net Margin Method: compare operating margins of tested party to comparable independent companies — used for management fees; (c) document analysis per BIR Transfer Pricing Documentation requirements (Revenue Regulations No. 02-2013)
Responsible (R): External Transfer Pricing Advisor
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 5–10 days (advisor)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1299_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1299_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1299_Task8" name="Pricing adjustment &amp; approval">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Pricing adjustment &amp; approval: (a) if benchmarking study indicates current intercompany pricing is outside arm&#x27;s-length range: Finance Controller proposes pricing adjustment to bring pricing within range; (b) CFO and VP Legal review adjustment for: (i) tax impact on each entity (some adjustments shift profit between entities), (ii) cash flow impact of revised pricing, (iii) compliance risk of current vs. proposed pricing; (c) approved pricing changes implemented in ERP: update intercompany pricing schedules, update AP/AR automation rules, update transfer pricing documentation file
Responsible (R): Finance Controller / CFO
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1–2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1299_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1299_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1299_Task9" name="Quarterly intercompany pricing monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quarterly intercompany pricing monitoring: Finance Controller monitors intercompany transactions quarterly: (a) actual transaction volumes vs. budget — significant variances may indicate pricing is incentivizing behavior inconsistent with arm&#x27;s-length principles, (b) entity-level profitability — if one entity consistently shows losses while the group is profitable, transfer pricing may need adjustment, (c) new intercompany transactions — any new service arrangement between entities must be priced at arm&#x27;s-length from inception
Responsible (R): Finance Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1299_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1299_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1299_Task10" name="Transfer pricing documentation maintenance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Transfer pricing documentation maintenance: (a) maintain Transfer Pricing Documentation (TPD) file per BIR requirements: (i) organizational structure, (ii) business overview, (iii) controlled transactions description, (iv) benchmarking analysis, (v) functional analysis (risks, assets, functions of each entity), (vi) financial statements of related parties; (b) TPD must be available within 30 days of BIR request; (c) annual update of TPD per benchmarking study; (d) retain documentation for 10 years per NIRC Sec. 235 (TRAIN-amended) BIR record retention rules
Responsible (R): Finance Controller / Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: 8 hours/year (ongoing maintenance)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1299_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1299_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1299_Task11" name="BIR audit response">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: BIR audit response: If BIR initiates transfer pricing audit: (a) VP Legal coordinates response; (b) Finance Controller compiles requested documentation within 30-day window; (c) External Transfer Pricing Advisor provides expert support; (d) negotiate with BIR examiners on any proposed adjustments; (e) if BIR issues assessment: VP Legal evaluates options — pay assessment, file protest, or appeal to Court of Tax Appeals
Responsible (R): VP Legal / Finance Controller
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Per audit event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1299_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1299_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1299_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1299_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1299_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-290 (ensure controlled execution — Consolidation &amp; Intercompany (PA-17.2).) | - operational: Finance Controller review and approval gate
Owner: Finance Controller</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1299_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1299_Annotation13" targetRef="W1299_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
