    <bpmn:process id="W_W1496" name="W1496. Intercompany Warehouse Service Fee Dispute Resolution, Rate Review &amp; Quarterly Settlement Agreement" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: One entity disputes the intercompany warehouse service fee charged by BuildRight Logistics, Inc.; also quarterly rate review cycle
Frequency: Quarterly rate review; disputes arising ~2–5 times/year (one register with W14)
Volume: Monthly intercompany service fees: PHP 50–80M across all DCs (per W1293); disputes typically involve PHP 200K–2M per incident
Owner: Intercompany Accountant
Participants: Intercompany Accountant, DC Controller, CFO (Logistics), CFO (Depot), Tax Manager
Source: workflow W1496 — Intercompany Warehouse Service Fee Dispute Resolution, Rate Review &amp; Quarterly Settlement Agreement</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1496_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1496_Lane1" name="DC Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1496_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1496_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1496_Lane2" name="Intercompany Accountant">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1496_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1496_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1496_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1496_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1496_Start4" name="One entity disputes the intercompany warehouse service fee charged by BuildRight…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1496_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1496_Task5" name="Monthly intercompany fee calculation &amp; invoicing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly intercompany fee calculation &amp; invoicing: (a) BRL&#x27;s DC Controller calculates monthly warehouse service fee per DC: (i) storage fee = pallet-days × rate per pallet per day; (ii) receiving fee = number of receipts × rate per receipt; (iii) picking fee = line items picked × rate per line; (iv) packing fee = orders packed × rate per order; (v) distribution fee = deliveries made × rate per delivery × distance zone; (b) calculation supported by WMS (Warehouse Management System) activity logs; (c) BRL generates intercompany invoice; (d) BRD&#x27;s Intercompany Accountant receives invoice and supporting detail
Responsible (R): DC Controller (BRL)
Accountable (A): CFO (BRL)
Duration: 2–3 days after month-end</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1496_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1496_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1496_Task6" name="Fee verification &amp; dispute initiation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Fee verification &amp; dispute initiation: (a) Intercompany Accountant (BRD) reconciles BRL invoice against: (i) WMS activity reports (pallet count, receipt count, pick lines, orders, deliveries); (ii) standard rate card per the Intercompany Service Agreement; (iii) prior month trends (are volumes consistent?); (b) discrepancies identified: (i) volume variances &gt; 5% from prior month without corresponding sales change; (ii) rate applied different from agreed rate card; (iii) charges for activities not performed (e.g., distribution fee for a month when BRL used third-party hauler at BRD&#x27;s cost); (c) if discrepancy found: dispute notice issued to BRL within 10 business days of invoice receipt
Responsible (R): Intercompany Accountant (BRD)
Accountable (A): CFO (BRD)
Duration: 1–2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1496_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1496_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1496_Task7" name="Dispute investigation &amp; resolution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Dispute investigation &amp; resolution: (a) both parties review WMS logs and supporting documents together; (b) common dispute causes: (i) WMS data error (pallets counted twice, ghost receipts); (ii) rate card misunderstanding (rate per unit vs. rate per case); (iii) unmetered activities (manual putaway not captured in WMS); (c) resolution options: (i) credit note from BRL for overcharge; (ii) supplementary invoice from BRL for undercharge; (iii) agreement to adjust methodology prospectively; (d) if parties cannot agree: CFO of both entities meet to resolve; (e) resolution documented with root cause and preventive action
Responsible (R): Intercompany Accountant (BRD) / DC Controller (BRL)
Accountable (A): CFO (both entities)
Duration: 1–5 days per dispute</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1496_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1496_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1496_Task8" name="Quarterly rate card review &amp; adjustment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quarterly rate card review &amp; adjustment: Quarterly: (a) Intercompany Accountant prepares rate card review: (i) actual costs incurred by BRL vs. rates charged to BRD; (ii) BRL profit margin on intercompany services (must be within arm&#x27;s-length range per Transfer Pricing Documentation); (iii) volume trends affecting unit costs (economies of scale); (iv) any new cost components (new DC, new service, labor rate changes); (b) rate adjustments proposed if actual cost recovery deviates &gt; 5% from target; (c) adjusted rate card approved by both VPs Finance; (d) Tax Manager reviews adjusted rates for transfer pricing compliance; (e) updated rate card effective following quarter
Responsible (R): Intercompany Accountant / Tax Manager
Accountable (A): CFO (both entities)
Duration: 1–2 days/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1496_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1496_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1496_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1496_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1496_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-290 (ensure controlled execution — Consolidation &amp; Intercompany (PA-17.2).) | - operational: CFO mediation and documented resolution for significant IC disputes, with outcome logged to the IC dispute register
Owner: Intercompany Accountant</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
